&lt;p&gt;The Cashiering team’s mission is to ensure accurate, timely movement of funds across customer brokerage and retirement accounts while delivering a compliant, high-quality client experience. We operate with ethics and precision at the center of everything we do to protect our customers&#39; assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team works closely with partners in Compliance, Operations, and Technology to streamline cashiering processes. We foster a supportive, collaborative environment where team members work together to solve complex operational challenges! Our collective goal is to build trusted, scalable financial processes that support Robinhood&#39;s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Cashiering Specialist, you will manage high-volume cashiering workflows—primarily reviewing money movement requests, including ACH, check, wire, and other brokerage transactions—serving as a key operational link between advisors, clients, custodians, and internal partners. In this position, you will serve as quality assurance overview of transactions with high accuracy and efficiency while adhering to strict regulatory requirements including AML, and OFAC review. You will collaborate daily with advisors and internal operations teams to resolve inquiries and transaction discrepancies. Your work directly impacts the customer experience by ensuring that fund movements are completed seamlessly. This role provides an excellent opportunity to expand your knowledge of financial markets and back-office operations!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Westlake, TX or Clearwater, FL office,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;with in-person attendance expected 5 days per week during the 90-day onboarding period. After onboarding, in-person attendance is expected at least 3 days a week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
