&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review a high volume of money movement requests efficiently, and in line with internal policies and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage daily transaction queues to meet strict deadlines and service-level expectations, researching and resolving discrepancies and inquiries from initial intake to final resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safeguard the firm by enforcing AML and OFAC requirements and reviewing transactions for adherence to SOPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our clearing firm and internal teams (Operations, Compliance, Technology, Advisor Services) to facilitate transactions, resolve issues, and support collaborative projects across these departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to continuous improvement by identifying opportunities to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and client experience within cashiering operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of asset movement procedures, workflows, and regulatory considerations, along with a basic understanding of financial markets and the securities industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and organization, with the ability to manage multiple priorities at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, professional communication skills, including excellent data entry, written, and verbal communication, and comfort engaging with clients and advisors over the phone.&lt;/li&gt;
