&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Money Customer Experience&lt;/strong&gt; team is responsible for providing our customers with the best experience possible while using our product. We collaborate closely within the team, leadership, and other support functions to ensure our customers have the best experience with our products and the services we offer. We serve as dedicated customer advocates, actively highlighting key product features and benefits to continually enhance and advance our services. We also build and maintain the tools necessary to provide exemplary service in each interaction. Our high-performing team is dedicated to supporting customers and ensuring their satisfaction!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Customer Experience Associate with Money&lt;/strong&gt;, you will serve as a subject matter expert on our Credit Card and Banking products and customer support processes. You will be the front-line expert responsible for assisting our cardholders with their most challenging inquiries. In this role, you will independently navigate complex inquiries, leveraging your subject matter expertise, departmental guidelines, and a compassionate, empathetic approach to resolve cardholder concerns with care and efficiency. Your work will directly impact customer trust and help drive the long-term success of our financial products!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Denver, CO, and Westlake, TX offices, with in-person attendance expected 5 days per week during the 6-week onboarding period. After onboarding, in-person attendance is expected at least 3 days a week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
