&lt;li&gt;Bring deep customer empathy and a passion for providing exceptional customer service to every cardholder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply critical thinking and problem-solving skills to remain adaptable as support processes evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate details independently, escalate issues appropriately, and identify emerging trends that may indicate product bugs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow continuously as our banking and credit card services expand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an advocate for our products and services, driving continuous improvement based on customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess 1+ years of customer service, financial services or contact center support experience, or equivalent demonstrated through one or a combination of the following: work experience, training, military experience, education.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a basic understanding of financial products, or a strong willingness to learn about them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show familiarity with text, email, and phone-based customer support channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply basic working knowledge of Salesforce or similar customer relationship management (CRM) platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
