&lt;p class=&quot;pw&quot;&gt;The Fraud Investigations team helps protect customers and the platform by reviewing suspicious activity, confirming what happened, and taking action to reduce risk. As a Fraud Investigation Analyst, you’ll review fraud alerts, analyze transactional and behavioral signals, and document outcomes in line with internal policy and regulatory requirements. You’ll also route higher-risk cases to the right partners and help limit customer impact through timely, accurate investigations—your work directly supports trust and safety across Robinhood!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pw&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Denver, CO and Westlake, TX office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pw&quot;&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shifts Available: &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;10:30am-7pm (local time)&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Days off: Wednesday/Thursday &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;6am-2:30pm (local time) &lt;br&gt;Days off: Tuesday/Wednesday&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;b&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and investigate fraud alerts to assess potential fraudulent activity using common fraud patterns and investigation steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze transactional and behavioral data to make risk-based decisions and complete clear, well-supported case documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily alert and case volume to meet quality and service-level targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, engineering, legal, compliance, vendor partners, and financial crime teams to gather information and escalate cases when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring fraud trends and suggest specific process improvements based on investigation outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
