&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;b&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0–2 years of experience in fraud investigations or related financial crime, risk, compliance, or operations work, with exposure to account takeovers, identity theft, or money movement fraud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written documentation skills and the ability to explain decisions using evidence from account activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and comfort working with multiple data points (transactions, device signals, behavioral indicators)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize work, manage queue volume, and meet defined quality and productivity goals&lt;/li&gt;
