&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Crimes (FinCrimes) Sanctions team plays a critical role in protecting Robinhood and its customers by identifying, investigating, and mitigating sanctions-related risks across our products and global operations. The team supports a rapidly evolving business, including cryptocurrency, brokerage, and money movement activities, while maintaining compliance with applicable U.S. and international sanctions requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Sanctions Crypto Investigator &lt;/strong&gt;you will be responsible for investigating potential sanctions exposure associated with cryptocurrency transactions, digital asset wallets, and customer activity. You will leverage blockchain analytics, investigative tools, and sound risk-based judgment to identify potential sanctions violations, assess complex transaction activity, and document defensible investigative conclusions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Denver, CO, Westlake, TX, or New York NY office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct thorough investigations of cryptocurrency-related sanctions alerts, including customer screening matches, deposits, withdrawals, wallet addresses, and blockchain transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage blockchain analytics tools, including TRM Labs or similar platforms, to evaluate direct and indirect sanctions exposure, trace transaction activity, and identify potential sanctions evasion typologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and disposition potential matches against OFAC and other applicable sanctions lists, ensuring timely, accurate, and well-documented investigative decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate potential sanctions violations, including transactions or assets that may require blocking, rejecting, or additional regulatory review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear, concise, and comprehensive investigative narratives, supporting documentation, and escalation recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor emerging cryptocurrency sanctions risks, regulatory developments, and illicit finance typologies to support ongoing risk identification and mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Compliance, Legal, Engineering, Product, and other FinCrimes teams to resolve complex investigations and enhance sanctions screening capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve investigative workflows, screening effectiveness, operational efficiency, and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with regulatory examinations, internal and external audits, quality assurance reviews, and management reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain adherence to established procedures, regulatory requirements, and internal service-level expectations while managing investigative workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in financial crimes, sanctions investigations, AML compliance, or a related field within financial services, fintech, cryptocurrency, or another regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience investigating cryptocurrency transactions and assessing financial crimes or sanctions-related risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of blockchain technology, digital asset transactions, wallet addresses, and cryptocurrency transaction flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using blockchain analytics tools such as TRM Labs, Chainalysis, Elliptic, or comparable platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of OFAC sanctions regulations, sanctions screening requirements, and common sanctions evasion methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting complex investigations, evaluating potential true positive matches, and preparing clear, defensible investigative documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills, with the ability to assess complex information and make sound, risk-based decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate investigative findings and recommendations effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain a high degree of accuracy in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset and willingness to partner across teams to solve problems and improve existing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards of integrity, professionalism, and discretion when handling confidential or sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
