&lt;p&gt;TradePMR is Robinhood&#39;s custody and technology platform for registered investment advisors (RIAs). Our integration ecosystem spans core technology partners, specialized workflow and TAMP partners, and a broader network of consultants, recruiters, and capital providers. You&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Engineering, Legal and Compliance, Marketing, Business Development, and the tactical integrations team. It&#39;s a collaborative group focused on advisor success and on building partnerships that last!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Strategic Partnerships &amp;amp; Integrations owns TradePMR&#39;s external-facing relationships with technology partners and advisor firms across the integration ecosystem. The tactical integrations team handles vendor onboarding, data feeds, and technical implementation. You&#39;ll decide which partnerships matter most and who we should build them with. You&#39;ll advise enterprise RIAs and breakaway teams, host partner events, negotiate special agreements, and equip our sales teams with accurate partner collateral. You&#39;ll also bring partner and client insight into integration roadmap discussions, shaping priorities through influence and input rather than build ownership. This is a business and partnerships role, not a product or engineering role, and your impact will show up in the strength of our advisor and partner relationships!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Tampa, FL and Clearwater, FLoffice(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a direct advisor to enterprise RIAs and breakaway teams evaluating custody transitions and platform fit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and run Transition Sandbox walkthroughs, live demo environments for prospective and transitioning firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted point of contact for advisor firms navigating the TradePMR integration ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the Partner Resource Hub, including custodial comparison sheets, integration guides, and platform one-pagers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip Practice Management and Sales with current, accurate partner and integration collateral, and keep internal teams informed of live and upcoming integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute the Center of Influence (COI) engagement cadence, including monthly strategy touchpoints, quarterly briefings, and virtual executive roundtables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up and run the COI Advisory Council, spanning consulting, technology, M&amp;amp;A, and recruiting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly own relationships with core technology partners and specialized workflow and TAMP partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Marketing and Business Development on adjacent COI relationships, such as transition consultants, M&amp;amp;A advisors, capital providers, breakaway recruiters, and compliance consultants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and represent TradePMR at flagship partner events, and own regional VIP dinners and executive roundtables, including guest lists, briefing content, and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate custom commercial terms with strategic partners, such as portfolio-wide custodial fee schedules, custom API reporting SLAs, and enterprise onboarding SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Compliance, and Finance on sign-off for non-standard agreements, using a template-first approach and escalating to custom terms only where justified&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface partner and client integration requests and pain points into Product and Engineering prioritization discussions&lt;/li&gt;
