&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily operations for an expanding international and domestic contracted physical security officer and emergency response force&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and put into effect policies for the safety and protection of our global operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and be responsible for formal training programs for security officer roles including, standard operating procedures, incident response protocols, communication plans, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with team members across different areas to set up security protocols for domestic and international office expansions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Display unwavering dedication to upholding the highest ethical standards, demonstrating a track record in managing highly confidential and sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement an event security program for large international marketing events/product launches and also manage internal employee events. Develop event security plan frameworks alongside key partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for facility risk assessments and propose key risk-management actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate efforts with cross-functional partners on projects including the response to security concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate as a key member of the Crisis Management Program supporting incident response plans, emergency action plans, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver core security solutions, alternatives and recommendations in support of Executives&lt;/li&gt;
