&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Prediction Markets&lt;/strong&gt; team at Robinhood is building the backend infrastructure that powers event contracts — giving everyday people access to markets that were once reserved for institutions. We&#39;re the fastest-growing product line at Robinhood, having recently surpassed stock and crypto trading revenues, and we&#39;re scaling fast! Our team thrives at the intersection of financial markets, real-time systems, and high-stakes product moments like NFL, NBA, and election cycles. We value engineering excellence, ownership at every level, and building with both speed and craft!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Staff Backend Engineer to join us at a pivotal moment — as we transition from a scrappy 0→1 team into a scaled, excellence-driven engineering org. In this role, you&#39;ll own the technical roadmap for critical backend systems, identify gaps, and drive architectural improvements that can support exponential growth. You&#39;ll collaborate closely with product, engineering leadership, and your cross-functional partners to ensure our infrastructure is ready for what&#39;s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our &lt;strong&gt;Menlo Park, CA and New York, NY &lt;/strong&gt;office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical roadmap for core Prediction Markets backend systems — identifying gaps, setting priorities, and driving execution across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build highly scalable, low-latency backend services that support real-time trading and event resolution at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering excellence initiatives: code quality, reliability, observability, and system resilience across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, platform, and other engineering teams to align technical direction with business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and level up engineers across the team, setting the technical bar and fostering a culture of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to hiring, onboarding, and shaping the engineering culture as the team scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of backend engineering experience, with a strong track record at IC6 / Staff Engineer scope or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading large-scale, distributed systems — designing for high availability, performance, and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with or genuine interest in prediction markets, sports betting, fantasy sports, trading platforms, or financial exchange systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical leadership skills — you&#39;ve driven engineering excellence roadmaps and influenced cross-functional outcomes without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills; comfortable engaging with product, leadership, and engineering stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2C product experience and an understanding of what it means to build for millions of end users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
